---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Drawbridge: free, private tools for assessment work."
>
  <div class="grid gap-8">
    <div class="grid gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">About</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">What Drawbridge is and why it exists.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 text-foreground">
      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Purpose</h2>
        <p>
          Drawbridge is a collection of small, single-purpose tools for assessment work. It is built around a simple
          idea: useful utilities should not require an account, a subscription, or a network connection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Privacy by design</h2>
        <p>
          Every tool runs entirely in your browser. There is no server processing your files, no analytics tracking your
          actions, and no database storing your work. Once the site is loaded, it works offline and can be installed as
          a progressive web app.
        </p>
        <p>
          For high-stakes assessment data, this means you can use Drawbridge without sending information anywhere. Close
          the tab and nothing remains.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Open and free</h2>
        <p>
          Drawbridge is free to use. It is primarily built for personal use, but others are welcome to use it if they
          find it helpful.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
